# UI inspiration — core memory

Curated, approved toolbox for building UI across Daymark (and other
projects that copy this rule). When you build or restyle UI, need an icon, a
font, a background, a logo, a generated image, or motion — **reach for the
matching resource below first** rather than inventing from scratch.

Human-readable copy (portable to other repos): `docs/ui-inspiration.md`.

## Components & UI libraries

- **shadcn/ui** — https://ui.shadcn.com — beautiful, accessible React components (Radix + Tailwind), copy-paste + CLI. **Default choice when building front-end components.**
- **Watermelon UI** — https://ui.watermelon.sh — open-source, copy-paste UI components, no strings attached. **General UI component building.**
- **daisyUI (Blueprint)** — https://daisyui.com/blueprint/ — Tailwind CSS component library; **exposes an MCP server** — prefer interacting with it via MCP for elements.
- **HorizonX** — https://horizonx.so — premium UI & code library with full templates. **When you want a template / full layout to start from.**
- **OriginKit** — https://www.originkit.dev — animated component library for Framer/React, **available through MCP**. **Animated backgrounds and animated UI for sites.**

## Backgrounds & patterns

- **Pattern Monster** — https://pattern.monster — customizable SVG patterns. **When custom SVG objects, backgrounds, or tiled images are needed.**
- **Pryzm** — https://pryzm.design — generate unique backgrounds in seconds. **When you need a one-of-a-kind background.**
- **OriginKit** (above) — for *animated* backgrounds.

## Icons

- **Iconify** — https://iconify.design — home of open-source icon sets (thousands, many families). **Default source for icons.**

## Fonts & typography

- **Not Your Type** — https://www.notyourtype.nl/typefaces/ — uncommon typefaces + a font builder. **Fetch for font inspiration / distinctive typography.**

## Logos & brand

- **Logo Diffusion** — https://logodiffusion.com — turn prompts / sketches / images into polished logos. **When we need to create a logo or brand mark.**

## Image / poster / character generation

- **Ideogram** — https://ideogram.ai — strong at text-in-image. **Fancy posters, character art, placeholder art.**
- **Krea** — https://www.krea.ai — generate, enhance, and edit images, video, or 3D meshes. **Generate new content from the info we already have.**

## Animation & motion

- **Casberry Particles** — https://particles.casberry.in — beautiful animation builder + AI prompt generator. **When generating animations, movement, flow, or dynamic motion in a site.**
- **OriginKit** (above) — animated components/backgrounds via MCP.

## Effects & stylization

- **Ditther** — https://www.ditther.com — dither, ASCII & halftone effects for images & video. **Pixel/ASCII-art style treatments.**

## How to use this memory

- **Match by intent** (component → shadcn/Watermelon; icon → Iconify; background → Pattern Monster/Pryzm; motion → Casberry/OriginKit; logo → Logo Diffusion; poster/art → Ideogram/Krea; font → Not Your Type; effect → Ditther; template → HorizonX/daisyUI).
- **Prefer MCP where available** (daisyUI, OriginKit): if their MCP server is configured for the run, use it; otherwise follow the site's copy-paste flow.
- **Stack note (Daymark):** the Daymark app currently uses React 19 + Vite + Motion (framer) with a hand-authored dark, cinematic CSS design system — it does **not** yet use Tailwind. shadcn / daisyUI / Watermelon are Tailwind-based, so adopting their components means adding Tailwind first; otherwise port the markup and restyle with the existing design tokens. Keep the aurora-accent, glass, Fraunces-display / Inter-UI aesthetic consistent.
- **Attribution/licensing:** check each source's license before shipping generated logos/art or bundling assets.

## Reusing across projects & maintenance

- To reuse in another cloud project, copy this file to that repo's `.cursor/rules/` (and `docs/ui-inspiration.md`).
- When you discover a new inspiration/tool, add it here under the right category with a one-line "use when" so the memory stays current.
